/** What each update brought, the newest first (the Changelog tab). */
val CHANGELOG: String = listOf(
    "# Changelog",
    "",
    "What's new in each update of Radon Player, the newest at the top. Everything the app does is in **Features**.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.19 · November 2026",
    "- **Updates always install over Radon Player Next:** 3.2.18's release was built as the other app (\"Radon Player\", a different app to Android), so Update in Settings couldn't install it and the file from GitHub installed beside Radon Player Next, without your settings and stats. Every release is now Radon Player Next, the same app, as RadonPlayer-Next.apk: it installs over the one you have and keeps everything. Update also checks the file is for this same app before installing, and turns down one that isn't instead of installing it beside it.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.18 · November 2026",
    "- **Repeated lines tick on their own:** on a lyrics card, ticking a line that's sung more than once (a chorus line) ticked every copy of it and put it on the card only once. Each line now ticks on its own, so you can put the same line on the card twice.",
    "- **Lyrics cards take up to 25 lines** (were 15). With more than 15 the card is taller (story-sized, 1080×1920) and the words get smaller as you tick more, so they always fit.",
    "- **Crossfade no longer repeats the end of a song:** for the fade, a second player takes over the ending song while the next one comes in. It started a moment after it was told to, so it was a little behind, and at the handover you heard the last half second or so again (a word sung twice) before the fade began. It's now lined up to the exact spot you're hearing (silently, before it takes over), so the song just fades out where it is. If it can't be lined up in time, that one change happens without a fade rather than repeat anything.",
    "- **True bit-perfect on Samsung and other phones:** Bit-perfect used Android's own bit-perfect mode, which only some phones have (Pixels do; Samsungs don't, for any DAC), so on those it was Android's mix, and it wrongly said your DAC didn't support it. Now, where Android has no bit-perfect mode, the app takes the USB DAC over and streams each song to it itself, the way USB Audio Player Pro does: at the song's own sample rate, its samples untouched (16-bit and 24-bit music exactly as in the file). Allow Radon Player to use the DAC once when Android asks (tick \"always\" when you plug it in and it isn't asked again). While it plays, the phone's volume buttons set the DAC's own volume, so the music stays bit-perfect at any volume, and other apps and notifications aren't heard through the DAC. Settings › Bit-perfect says what the DAC is getting. Turning bit-perfect off, unplugging the DAC or closing the app hands it back to Android.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.17 · November 2026",
    "- **Wrapped opens when Last.fm is down:** when Last.fm (or the way to it) was busy for a moment (\"HTTP 503… connection timeout\"), Wrapped showed only an error. Every request to Last.fm is now asked again twice, a moment apart, before it counts as failed, and if Last.fm still isn't answering, Wrapped opens from the scrobbles saved on this device and your imports (saying so), instead of not at all. Try again later for the newest scrobbles. The DJ and Most played keep their counts through it too.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.16 · November 2026",
    "- **No more songs skipped after a crossfade:** after a crossfade, the ending song plays on silently in the player while the next one loads. If loading took a while, that song's end counted as the next song ending, so the next song was skipped before you heard it. Only the song really playing counts now.",
    "- **\"Ran on past its end\" no longer misfires:** the check for a song that keeps going past its end (so Repeat one never gets stuck) compared the next song with the last song's clock while the next was loading, and trusted the player's length even when it was a little short (some MP3s and streams), so it logged nearly every song and could cut one off early. It now only looks at the song really in the player and uses the song's real length. If it ever happens again, Problems says how far in it was and how long the song is.",
    "- **The DJ knows every song you've played:** it could call a song you've played new to you (\"you haven't played these yet\"), because it matched your plays by the song's full artist (\"A & B\", \"A feat. B\") while Last.fm and your imports have it under the lead artist. It now matches the way Most played does, so the plays come from Last.fm and your imports (the plays here only when there are none of those at all), and a song you've ever played in the app is never called new either.",
    "- **Switch it up from your headphones, the reliable way:** pause with your headphones, then Next (a double tap on most earbuds): with the DJ on, it switches it up and starts playing. The quadruple tap (two double taps) didn't work, since earbuds wait after each tap to see if more are coming, so the two Nexts came too far apart and just skipped two songs; it's gone. While playing, Next skips one song as always. The same goes for Next on the lock screen, in the car and on the PC's media keys.",
    "- **Loudness compensation starts off:** on a new install, Loudness compensation (Settings › Sound) is off; the other sound switches stay on from the start. If you've already been using the app, nothing changes for you.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.15 · November 2026",
    "- **Nine new kinds of DJ set:** Artist spotlight (one artist you love, their big ones and a couple of deeper cuts), Album moment (three in a row from an album you play a lot, in the album's order), On this day (what you played this week one, two or more years ago), Decade trip (your songs from one decade, read from their tags, a different decade each time), One-hit wonders (artists you have only a song or two from), Never skipped (songs you've always heard to the end), Second chances (songs you usually skip, in case the mood's right today), Unreleased corner (songs in your Unreleased folders) and Streaks (songs you've played on four or more days this week). A kind that can't be made from your music (no Unreleased folder, say) is just left out.",
    "- **More variety in every set:** no artist twice in a row, and at most two songs by one artist in a set (but for an artist's own sets). The kinds you haven't heard lately are likelier to come up next, and never the same kind twice in a row. Sets pick from all your music now, not just your top 300 songs: every song you've played (the most played still likelier) and every song of yours you haven't played yet, plus more of each year's and hour's.",
    "- **Every set flows by mood:** the songs after the first are ordered by their moods, building up from a calm start and easing down from a loud one.",
    "- **The DJ has more to say:** more lines for every kind of set; new facts (a song you've played every day this week, what you played a year ago this week, how long you've followed an artist, your big new artist this month, this month's plays, a song that fits your mood lately); milestones (a song's 100th play, its 500th…) always announced; greetings for Friday night, the weekend and Monday morning, and now and then a word about the day before a set.",
    "- **A word between songs:** now and then, once a set at most, the DJ says something before a song in the middle of a set: that it's your number one, that you've never skipped it, that you only found it last week, or a milestone it's reaching. It's made while the song before plays, so it's said straight away (that song ends without a crossfade).",
    "- **YouTube songs download in FLAC:** a song from YouTube Music is often its music video, a little longer than the recording, and the match on Tidal turned down anything more than 6 seconds off, so it downloaded from YouTube (Opus 160 kbps) instead. Now a YouTube song may be up to half a minute off when its title and artist match closely, so it comes from Tidal in FLAC. The same match is used when a song streams, so the DJ's new finds from YouTube Music play from Tidal in FLAC too (YouTube only when Tidal really hasn't the song).",
    "- **YouTube downloads are AAC, not Opus:** a song only YouTube has is saved as its best AAC (.m4a, 256 kbps where YouTube offers it, else 128), which plays and tags everywhere like your other M4As; Opus only when YouTube has no AAC of it.",
    "- **Upgrade in Downloads:** your YouTube downloads got again from Tidal in FLAC where Tidal has them, else (the Opus ones) as YouTube's AAC; each old file is deleted once the new one is in.",
    "- **Downloads stay in Downloads:** when the app started, a download the phone wouldn't open for a moment (a permission or a busy file provider) was taken off the list, though its file was still there. Only one whose file is really gone is taken off now.",
    "- **Crossfade without a cut:** the ending song began fading the moment the next one was asked for, but the next only came up once it had loaded, so for that moment both were low, which sounded like a cut. Now the ending plays on at full until the next song is really playing, and then one fade takes the ending down as the next comes up, in step (equal power, so it never dips). Skipping during a crossfade stops the ending at once.",
    "- **Car always wins (Settings › Playback, under Newest Bluetooth device wins, the phone):** a failsafe: whenever the car is connected (its Bluetooth or Android Auto), it has the music and its EQ, whatever headphones are connected too. The app learns the car's Bluetooth name the first time Android Auto starts with it (and knows names that are plainly a car's). Ignore Bluetooth devices still comes first.",
    "- **Newest Bluetooth device wins sticks with the car:** getting in the car with an earbud set down, the music went to the car, then back to the earbud a couple of seconds later, for two reasons: Android Auto starting a moment after the car's Bluetooth counted as a newer device, and an earbud dropping out for a moment and coming back counted as newly connected. Now Android Auto and the car's Bluetooth are one device, and a device back within a minute and a half keeps the time it first came, so the car keeps the music.",
    "- **Switch it up from your headphones:** while the DJ plays, tap your headphones four times (two double taps, which they send as two Nexts) and it switches it up instead of skipping twice. One double tap still skips one song. Works on the phone and on the PC.",
    "- **Refresh in Downloads:** ↻ Refresh beside the sort reads your downloads again, so one that didn't show up comes in.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.14 · November 2026",
    "- **Switch it up on Now playing and the queue:** while the DJ plays, ✦ at the top of Now playing (beside the set button) and Switch it up over the queue's Continue Playing start a new kind of set at once.",
    "- **Next is full size again:** in layouts with a side rail, the row of Previous, Play and Next ran out of room and Next was squeezed into a tiny icon in its corner. The three now shrink together to fit (all the same size), and an icon that's ever squeezed is drawn whole in the middle.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.13 · November 2026",
    "- **The DJ is instant:** its first set is made ahead in the background while the DJ is off (from where it played last, made again every half hour), line and all, so tapping DJ starts it at once. While it plays, three more sets are kept ready, each with its line already made, so Switch it up and the set button change category at once, however fast you go, and the next set at the end of the queue is one of them too. Each one used is replaced in the background.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.12 · November 2026",
    "- **Newest Bluetooth device wins (Settings › Playback, under Ignore Bluetooth devices):** with two Bluetooth devices connected (an earbud you set down in the truck, then the truck), the one that connected last has the music, the DJ and its own EQ, instead of the one that was there first. Android Auto counts as a device. They work together: a device you ignore never gets the music, even when it's the newest. Apps can't disconnect a device, so the other one stays connected for calls, but nothing plays on it. On the PC too.",
    "- **Ignore Bluetooth devices works with Android Auto:** with the car ignored, Android Auto (wired or wireless) still took the music, since its sound isn't a Bluetooth output. Now the car's screen keeps the map, calls and the rest, while the music and the DJ's voice play on your headphones (Bluetooth ones you haven't ignored, else wired). It knows the car by its Bluetooth name (also when it's only connected for calls), or pick Android Auto itself in the list. With no headphones connected, the music stays on the car.",
    "- **No more music stopping by itself in the background:** after any pause (one of the DJ's, a call, a moment's pause of yours), Android took the app out of the foreground, and with the screen off it wouldn't let it back in when the music went on (\"startForegroundService() not allowed\"), so the music stopped. The app now stays a foreground player for 10 minutes after a pause, so Play from your headphones, the car or the lock screen, and the DJ's next set, always carry on. Paused longer than that, it lets go as before.",
    "- **The DJ keeps going on its own:** between sets the music was paused while the DJ's line was made and said, and with the screen off Android could take the app out of the background in that pause, so the DJ stopped by itself. Nothing pauses now: the set's first song waits at its start under the line with its volume all the way down, so you hear only her (Now playing's time moves while she talks), then plays from the top. A crossfade's ending song is cut off when she starts, and with Bit-perfect (which can't turn a song down) the song waits paused as before. Only you stop it.",
    "- **The DJ talks straight away:** the next set's line is made in the background while the current set plays, so when a set begins she starts talking at once instead of after a long wait for the natural voice (or ElevenLabs). Switch it up is instant too: a set is always made ahead for it, line and all.",
    "- **The DJ never gets stuck between sets:** skipping with your headphones' buttons into a new set could leave it paused with the DJ silent, and the headphones' Play did nothing (only the app's Play got it going). Play from the headphones, the car or the lock screen now does exactly what the app's Play does: a line that never came out is said again, a set it hadn't introduced gets its line, and one it was still picking goes on when it's ready (trying again if the lookup failed, rather than stopping). If the voice ever doesn't finish, the music starts anyway, and Pause on your headphones while the DJ talks stops her too.",
    "- **The DJ's play counts are your real ones:** it counted an artist's and a song's plays only from the plays with a time the phone had read, so it could say Juice WRLD had 75 plays when you have far more. Everything the DJ goes by (its counts, sets and facts) now comes from Last.fm and your Spotify, Apple Music, Deezer, YouTube Music and Tidal imports, an artist's plays under one name. The plays counted in the app are only used when there's nothing from Last.fm or an import at all (they still keep a song you just played from coming straight back).",
    "- **Skips never keep songs out of the DJ:** the DJ left out songs you'd skipped three times or more (more often than you heard them out). Skips don't change what it plays now (you may just not be in the mood for a song); they're only counted, for Skips and for the DJ to tell you about: your most skipped song, songs you've never skipped, how many you skipped this week and in all.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.11 · November 2026",
    "- **Lyrics files (.lrc) (Settings › Scanner › Lyrics & moods):** saves a .lrc file beside each song that has lyrics in its file, with the song's file name (its timed lines when it has them, else its words, with the title, artist and album at the top), so any player, and the folder wherever you copy it, has them. Works on the PC and on the phone (with All files access); songs with a .lrc already are left as they are.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.10 · November 2026",
    "- **Wrapped and lyrics card styles in pictures:** Settings › Personalization's Wrapped style and Lyrics card style menus show what each one looks like (a slide of Wrapped in that style and your look, and a lyrics card in that style): tap one on the phone to see it under it, point at one on the PC.",
    "",
    "- **Syncs never touch covers:** Tags & covers match is now Tags match: a sync only fills in missing titles, artists, albums, album artists, genres, years and track numbers (moods sync their own way). It never writes, replaces or takes off a cover; a song with none gets one from Songs without covers.",
    "",
    "- **Every scanned song's moods go into its file:** Scan moods worked a song's moods out from what it remembered of it, which could be from before the song was scanned (no moods yet), so it wrote the words' reading into the file but not the moods: about two thirds of your songs. It works them out fresh now, and the Moods tab shows how many scanned songs still need their moods written, with Write moods into the files to do it.",
    "- **Prevent auto mood scans (Settings › Scanner):** on, the moods stop being edited: every mood already in your files stays as it is and still shows, but no song is scanned (a new one you add waits until you turn it off) and nothing more is written into any file's moods or taken from your other device.",
    "- **Prevent album cover changes (Settings › Scanner):** on, no sync, scan or auto tagger changes, puts in or takes off a cover in a song's file; only one you pick yourself (the Tagger's Cover) does. Scan tags, Single scan, Fix albums and artists and Covers from folders say so while it's on.",
    "- **Save covers into folders (Settings › Scanner):** one picture of each album, EP and single saved in its folder beside its songs (cover.jpg, or one for each release when a folder holds several), from a song's own cover, so a lost cover can always be put back.",
    "- **Covers from folders (Settings › Scanner):** each song with no cover in its file gets its folder's picture (its release's own), so a whole album has its cover again in one go.",
    "- **A cover you pick goes into your own files:** picking a cover (the Tagger's Cover, Pick a cover, Songs without covers) for your own songs kept it in the app on that device only, so the phone never had the covers you'd picked on the PC (your unreleased songs' covers were only ever in the PC app, never in their files). It now always goes into the songs' files (your own and the app's downloads, MP3, M4A, WAV, FLAC), so it goes wherever the files go; the song playing gets it as soon as another song starts (its file is in use while it plays). For covers picked before, Save covers into folders then Covers from folders on the PC puts them into the files.",
    "- **Unreleased left alone on the phone too:** the phone looked for the Unreleased folder in the wrong place, so a sync could still reach those songs there; it finds the song's real folder now.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.9 · November 2026",
    "- **Update works in Radon Player Next:** the test app's Update fetched the release's APK, which is the other app (Radon Player, not Radon Player Next), so Android refused it (INSTALL_FAILED_INVALID_APK, package inconsistent). Radon Player Next now updates to the newest Next build whenever a new release is out.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.8 · November 2026",
    "- **The DJ keeps DJing when you skip:** a skip near the end of the DJ's queue set off ∞ (Autoplay), which filled the queue with a radio of streams: songs that aren't the DJ's (no sets, so it went quiet), and not only yours. With the DJ on, ∞'s radio never starts now: skip to the end of its queue and it goes on to its next set (waiting for it if it's still picking), and introduces it as always.",
    "- **Only my songs means only yours:** with the DJ's Only my songs on, every set is your songs alone (a stream it found never gets in), and asking for something that isn't in your music finds nothing rather than playing it from everywhere.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.7 · November 2026",
    "- **Covers stay put on the phone:** WAVs are tagged on the phone the way the PC does it (by hand: their ID3 chunk, where the cover is, and LIST INFO, every other chunk kept), not through the tag library, which could read only a WAV's LIST INFO and write it back without its ID3 chunk, cover and all. Any other file whose cover the tag library drops while its other tags change gets it put straight back.",
    "- **Unreleased songs keep their covers:** the phone read the cover inside FLACs only, so to Tags & covers match every MP3, M4A and WAV there looked as if it had none, and each sync wrote the PC's cover into it through the tag library (which could leave it with none at all). The phone now reads the cover in any file, a song that has one is never given another, and a folder named Unreleased is always left alone by a sync, on both devices, whether it's in Folders sync leaves alone or not.",
    "- **Filled-in tags are left alone:** Tags & covers match only fills in what a song is missing now (a tag with nothing in it, a cover when it has none); it never changes a tag that's filled in or replaces a cover. Tags change only when you edit them (the Tagger, Edit tags) or run a scan to change them. The genres the app looks up for its downloads with none aren't sent to your other device either.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.6 · November 2026",
    "- **Presets in pictures:** each Personalization preset shows what it looks like: Now playing (its look, effects and visualizers), a slide of Wrapped in its style and its lyrics card. Tap one in the menu (click on the PC) to see its pictures and swipe through them, then tap it again to put it on; on the PC they also show beside the menu as you point at one, and turn by themselves.",
    "- **Personalization Preset Shuffle:** a switch at the very top of Settings › Personalization puts on a different one of your favourite presets (★) every 5, 10, 15 or 30 minutes (Change every). It only shuffles favourites.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.5 · November 2026",
    "- **30 ready-made Personalization presets:** each a whole setup that goes together, in one tap: a look and theme, a layout, effects, Now playing's visualizer (Dual: one in the middle and one along the bottom) and its colour, Wrapped's style and a lyrics card style to match. Midnight drive, Northern lights, Golden hour, Cherry blossom, Deep ocean, Misty woods, Desert mirage, Old TV, Code rain, Cotton candy, Thunderstorm, First snow, Galaxy quest, Lava lamp, Notebook, Comic book, Vaporwave, Firefly meadow, Love letter, Concert night, Circuit, Autumn walk, Moonlight, Hyperspace, Cabin fire, Polka pop, Neon frame, Contours, Meteor night and Dream orbs.",
    "- **Yours marked:** the presets you saved show (yours) in the Personalization presets menu, so the ready-made ones and yours are easy to tell apart. Presets now keep the visualizer's colour too.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.4 · November 2026",
    "- **No made-up moods:** a song gets moods only from Scan moods, its file's MOOD tag, your own picks or your other device; the guess from the genre alone is gone. After Remove all moods the Moods tab is really empty until you scan (the genre guesses made it look as if moods were still in the files).",
    "- **Dual on Now playing:** Now playing's visualizer button has a Dual switch: pick one style for the middle (around the cover) and one for the bottom, and both play at once, no need to make your own. It's in Settings › Personalization too.",
    "- **Wrapped and lyrics card styles in Personalization:** Settings › Personalization has Wrapped style and Lyrics card style menus (they stay in Wrapped and the Lyrics card box too), so everything about how the app looks is in one place, and a Personalization preset now keeps the Dual visualizer, Wrapped's style and the lyrics card's style as well.",
    "- **Pine forest fixed:** the trees all stand on the bottom edge now (the back row used to float above it), each one solid tree of three tiers on a short trunk (no darker patches where the tiers overlap), sized to the space (no wall of trees in a small preview), and the effect takes its own colour when you pick one.",
    "- **All your personalization in backups and Sync:** your own looks, layouts, visualizers and colour blends, Wrapped styles, lyrics card styles, Personalization presets and now your saved colours too are all in backups, and each Sync adds the other device's to yours (one deleted on either is gone from both). Each device still wears its own look, theme and layout; pick a preset to put the same setup on the other one.",
    "- **One mood scan:** Scan moods, Full scan and Read moods from lyrics are one scan now. Scan moods hears each song whole and reads its words (by the AI when it's on), and only once both are done writes the song's moods (and its words' reading) into its file, so the sound always has its say before anything is written.",
    "- **Moods go into the files only from the scan:** the Write moods into the files tick is gone; nothing writes moods into your files but Scan moods (and moods you pick yourself in the Tagger).",
    "- **Scanned once:** the app keeps track of every song it has scanned and never scans it again; Settings › Reset mood and lyrics scans is the only way to start over. A song whose moods aren't in its file yet (the playing song, moods from your other device) just has them written by the next scan, with nothing heard again.",
    "- **Settings resets for the one scan:** Reset moods works the moods out again from what was heard and read (nothing heard again) and the next Scan moods writes them in; Reset sound scan and Remove all moods are followed by Scan moods too.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.3 · November 2026",
    "- **Artist pictures in Search:** artists found in Search show the same picture as on the Artists tab (the one you picked, or the one looked up), and the ones not looked up yet are looked up there.",
    "- **Lyrics card styles:** the Lyrics card box has a Style menu (by Save and the share buttons): Your look (as before), Now playing (the card as the Now playing screen looks with the Now playing look, in the cover's colours, whatever look is in use), 30 ready-made styles (Synthwave, Aurora night, Golden hour, Cherry blossom, Ocean deep, Old TV, Code rain, Galaxy, Comic book, Hyperspace and more), each with its own colours and effects, and the ones you make. Hold one or tap its ⋯ (right-click on the PC) to favourite it; yours can be edited or deleted there too. The one you pick stays for the next card.",
    "- **Make your own lyrics card:** Settings › Personalization › Make your own › New lyrics card: every colour (the background's top and bottom, the card behind the words, the words, the song name, the soft text, the Radon Player mark), how see-through the card is and its corners, bold or regular words and their size, a round cover, stars and any effects each in its own colour. Start from any ready-made style, Copy my look, Randomize, Randomize colours and Saved colours work there too, and the card shows as you go. Yours go to your other device at each Sync and into backups.",
    "- **Lyrics card with the Now playing look:** the card now looks like the Lyrics screen does with the Now playing look: black, the words in the cover's colour, with the stars and effects (they were left off).",
    "- **Dual volume:** a switch under the Equalizer's Boost (the same screen from Now playing). On (as before): a song with its own volume (Volume… in its menu) gets the Boost on top too. Off: a song with its own volume plays at just that volume, without the Boost; every other song keeps the Boost.",
    "- **Personalization presets:** Settings › Personalization has a Personalization presets menu and a Save as a preset button: it saves everything picked on the tab (look, theme, layout, the looks' own effects or the effects you picked and their colours, Now playing's visualizer) under a name, and picking a preset puts all of it back at once. Hold one or tap its ⋯ (right-click on the PC) to favourite, edit or delete it; Edit puts it on so you can change anything, then Save changes (or Save as new). Presets go to your other device at each Sync and into backups.",
    "- **Mood scans only when you tap them:** Scan moods no longer starts by itself after your music is scanned (or after a sync); Scan moods, Full scan and Read moods from lyrics each run only when you tap them. Moods already in your files are still noticed straight away.",
    "- **Remove all moods takes every one out:** each file is read again after its mood is taken off, and any mood still there (an MP3 tag with an extended header, an M4A's mood saved under another app's name, a FLAC with an ID3 tag in front, a file the usual writer couldn't replace) is blanked where it is, every other tag and the sound kept byte for byte. Files that still keep one are named in Settings › Problems, and moods from your other device wait until a Full scan has heard the songs here again, so a sync can't put the old ones back.",
    "- **Your own Wrapped:** Make your own › New Wrapped: pick its background, text, soft text and accent colours and a colour for each slide, the glow (and how strong), neon text, bold or light type, text size, spacing, corners, round covers and their size, bar thickness, tiles, and stars and effects behind every slide (each effect in its own colour). Randomize, Randomize colours and Saved colours work there too, and a slide in it shows as you go.",
    "- **Wrapped in your look:** Wrapped's Style menu has Your look: the slides take the app's look in use, its stars and effects too.",
    "- **Favourites in Wrapped's Style menu:** hold down a style (or its ⋯, or right-click) to favourite it; the ones you made can be edited or deleted there.",
    "- **30 more visualizers:** 15 along the bottom (City lights, Capsules, Hills, Steps, Needles, Ribbon, Dot bars, Flames, Tides, 8-bit, Bouncing balls, Meadow, Outlines, Curtain, Echoes) and 15 around the middle that come out of the cover's centre on Now playing, Full screen too (Orbits, Spiral, Polygons, Radar, Light rays, Atom, Mandala, Ripples, Supernova, Honeycomb, Heart, Sunflower, Vortex, Iris, Clockwork). They're in the Visualizer tab, Now playing's visualizer menu and Make your own visualizer.",
    "- **Visualizers come out of the cover's middle:** a visualizer drawn around a middle (Ring, Pulse, Starfield, Dual's middle style…) now always centres on the album cover on Now playing, in every layout, with Full screen on or off.",
    "- **Your own visualizers centre too:** one you made with Full screen on, from a style around a middle, now comes out of the cover's exact centre like the built-in ones (it's drawn from the cover itself), and the visualizer menu's previews put the cover in their middle.",
    "- **Starfield fills the screen:** with Full screen on, its stars fly from the cover's middle out to every edge of the screen, past the song's name and the buttons, Full screen on or not (yours made from Starfield too, Dual's middle as well).",
    "- **Dual, each its own way:** a Dual visualizer's bottom style has its own Shape it (mirror, upside down, reflection, glow, spin, strength) and its own colour, apart from the middle one's.",
    "- **Delete stays in the menu:** deleting one of yours in a menu asks right there (Yes, delete / Cancel) and the menu stays open.",
    "- **Everything you made is in its menu:** the list under Make your own is gone; your looks, layouts, visualizers, colour blends and Wrapped styles are in their own menus (hold or ⋯ to edit, favourite or delete; colour blends too now). Two with the same name get a number.",
    "- **Nothing under the phone's buttons:** the bottom of every menu and full-screen page stays above the phone's Back and Home buttons, so the last ones can be tapped.",
    "- **Your Wrapped's effects in its colours:** the effects on a Wrapped style you made (and its picture in Make your own Wrapped) are drawn in that style's own colours, not the app look's, so what you pick is what you see.",
    "- **Make your own Wrapped shows your changes:** its pictures now change the moment you change a colour, effect, type or anything else (they stayed on the first look before).",
    "- **The visualizer's Look's colour is your look's:** Look's colour on Now playing is your look's own colour now (it used to be turned round to a different colour); with the Now playing look it's still the cover's.",
    "- **The PC's mini player is Now playing made small:** your look's background, stars and effects (or the cover's colours with the Now playing look), Now playing's visualizer, the cover in your layout's shape and the song, with the seek bar and buttons under it in the look's colour.",
    "- **Rain that rains:** Rain and Code rain (and yours made from them, a Dual's bottom one too) fall down the whole of Now playing, not only the bottom.",
    "- **Effects: look first:** on the phone the first tap on an effect shows its picture; tap it again to put it on or off.",
    "- **Apple Music history imports a big download:** Apple's Play Activity file (hundreds of megabytes) is read a row at a time, straight from the zip, instead of all at once, which ran the phone out of memory (\"Failed to allocate…\"); and a stray quote mark inside a field (a 12\" mix) no longer swallows the rest of the file.",
    "- **Copy my look in Make your own Wrapped:** one tap takes your look's colours (background, text, accent, the slides in shades of it), its neon glow, stars and effects, to add your own effects and changes on top.",
    "- **Name your saved colours:** Save these colours asks for a name straight away; hold one of yours in Saved colours (or tap its ✎) to rename it. On the phone the list ends above the phone's buttons.",
    "- **Reset mood and lyrics scans (Settings):** Reset moods works every song's moods out again from what the scans already heard and read, dropping the moods a sync, a backup or the files brought, and rewrites them into your files, with no scanning. Reset sound scan has every song heard again (the lyrics readings kept). Clear my moods forgets the moods you picked yourself. Remove all moods takes every mood (and words' reading) out of every file and forgets everything, for a completely fresh Full scan. Only the MOOD tags ever change, nothing else in the files. The Moods tab's \"heard whole\" now counts only songs Full scan really heard, not ones that just have a mood in their file. Each asks if you're sure first. Moods you picked yourself stay.",
    "- **More moods per song:** a song that's been heard is now also in the other moods that fit it fairly well, not only its main one (never its opposite, like Happy and Sad, unless that's plain).",
    "- **30 more effects:** falling petals, autumn leaves, embers, lightning, comets, a meteor shower, a moon, a ringed planet, clouds, fog, a night sea, desert dunes, a pine forest, graph paper, polka dots, a checkerboard, plaid, a circuit board, contour lines, a starburst, a prism, sparkles, floating hearts, music notes, glowing orbs, a spiral galaxy, an old TV, glitch, warp speed and sunbeams. 61 in all, each in any colour.",
    "- **Use the scans' moods:** songs held to the one mood already in their file (another app's, your other device's or an older version's) now show a Moods tab button to use what the scans found for them instead, with nothing heard again that was heard; the files then get all their moods. Full scan now also hears songs whose mood the app wrote itself. A song not heard on this device uses the moods your other device found (from a sync) over the single one in its file.",
    "- **Dual's bottom style on the bottom edge:** with Full screen on, a Dual visualizer's bottom style stands right on the bottom of the screen, as a bottom style always does, not raised above it.",
    "- **The PC's mini player has Now playing's buttons:** the song with ☆ and ⋯, the seek bar, Shuffle · previous · play · next · Repeat, the volume, and the pill with the lyrics, the output and EQ and the queue (shown in the cover's place). Only Personalization isn't there; ↑ goes back to the big window.",
    "- **Every slide while you make your Wrapped:** Make your own Wrapped shows all your Wrapped's slides in the style you're making; swipe left and right (or ‹ ›) through them.",
    "- **Clear of the phone's buttons:** on the phone the menus open in a box that always ends above Back and Home (it scrolls inside), and Wrapped's slides (Share… too) stay above them.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.2 · November 2026",
    "- **Each device keeps its own look:** Sync no longer copies the look, theme, layout, visualizer choices or picked effects between the phone and the PC, so each can look different. The looks, layouts and visualizers you made still go to both: one made on the phone is on the PC after the next sync.",
    "- **Lyrics cards in your look:** a lyrics card now takes the look in use on that device: its background (and fade), its stars and effects, the lyrics on a rounded card like the Lyrics screen's (with a small LYRICS heading) and the song's name in its accent, with your own file's cover too. The Now playing look still uses the cover's colours.",
    "- **How long a mood scan takes:** Scan moods, Full scan, Read moods from lyrics, Rescan and writing into files each say about how long they'll take before you start (from how fast they went last time on this device), and while running they show the time left right beside how far they've got.",
    "- **Hold on the phone:** hold your finger on any look, theme, layout, effect or visualizer in its menu (or a style in the Visualizer tab): Favourite for every one, and Edit and Delete too for the ones you made, shown right under it, as right-click does on the PC. After a favourite moves to the top, holding or tapping always acts on the one under your finger. Each one also has a ⋯ at its right that opens the same choices with a tap.",
    "- **Wrapped's top singles and EPs fit:** a full top 15 shows as one list, like the top songs, so all of it fits on the phone's screen.",
    "- **Edit from the menu:** right-click (or hold) one of your own looks, layouts or visualizers in its menu and tap Edit: its maker opens with every setting it has, name included, ready to change.",
    "- **Tag any song on the phone:** the Tagger can now change your own songs' tags and covers on the phone too (FLAC, MP3, M4A, Ogg, WAV and more, each in its own format), not just the app's downloads. Android asks once: tap Allow in the Tagger and turn on All files access for Radon Player.",
    "- **Your own looks keep their effects:** the effects picked in Settings › Personalization › Effects now go with the ready-made looks only; a look you made shows the effects you gave it.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.1 · November 2026",
    "- **Picture menus stay open on the phone:** in Look, Theme, Layout, Now playing visualizer and Effects, a tap puts that one on and shows its picture right under it, and the menu stays open so you can try others. Back or a tap outside closes it. (Layout shows its picture as you tap and goes on when you close the menu, since a new layout redraws the whole screen.)",
    "- **Repeat one never gets stuck at the end:** a song whose player ran on past its end (or sat at -0:00) without saying it had finished now starts again on Repeat one, or moves on to the next song otherwise, within a second or two, on the phone and the PC.",
    "- **Visualizers keep moving on the phone:** every visualizer on screen (Now playing's, the Visualizer tab's, Make your own visualizer's) now shares one listener to the music, so one no longer freezes another; it follows each new song and starts listening again by itself if it goes quiet while music plays.",
    "- **Previews in a small window:** on the PC, with the window small and the menu at the right edge, a picture no longer flickers: it goes beside the menu where there's room, else under or over the one pointed at, never under the pointer.",
    "- **Your own looks, layouts and visualizers on every device:** Sync now puts together what you made on the phone and on the PC (each one kept, not one device's list swapping out the other's), and one you delete goes on both. Restoring a backup adds its looks, layouts and visualizers beside the ones you made on that device, on any device.",
    "- **Dual visualizers:** Make your own visualizer has a Dual switch. Start from greys out and two rows appear: one of the styles drawn in the middle and one of the styles along the bottom. Both play at once; on Now playing the middle one goes over the cover and the other along the bottom.",
    "- **Your own colours for every effect:** Pick an effect (in Make your own look, or Personalization › Effects) and its colour shows below; tap it to change its colour, or Look's colours to put it back.",
    "- **Randomize colours:** Make your own look, the colour blends and the effects' colours each have a Randomize colours button that changes only the colours, as a start to build on.",
    "- **Rain and snow over everything:** The Rain and Snow effects now fall over the seek bar and buttons too (taps still reach them).",
    "- **Favourites and right-click:** Right-click (or hold your finger on) a look, layout or visualizer in its menu: ★ Favourite puts it at the top of the list, and the ones you made can be deleted from there.",
    "- **Saved colours:** Make your own look and the colour blends have Save these colours and a Saved colours menu: your saved sets and 15 ready-made four-colour sets in each. Favourite any of them (★, to the top); yours can be deleted, the ready-made ones stay.",
    "- **Test the key always answers:** It says whether the key worked or not every time, even when Anthropic doesn't answer (after 25 seconds).",
    "- **Full screen visualizers on Now playing:** Make your own visualizer has a Full screen switch: Now playing then shows your visualizer over the whole screen, cover and all, just as the Visualizer tab draws it (the buttons still work under it), instead of around the cover or along the bottom. The maker's preview shows where the cover sits.",
    "- **Test the key shows its answer:** In Lyrics & moods, Test the key now says right under the button whether the key works (and tests the key in the box, even before Save), so the answer can't hide behind the settings.",
    "- **Randomize in every maker:** Make your own look, layout and visualizer each have a Randomize button that sets every choice at random (colours, fade, glow, stars and effects; the way round, the bar's buttons, the mini player, Now playing and every More choice; the style and its shaping, or a colour blend), as a start you can change.",
    "- **Every layout choice shows in its picture:** Make your own layout's picture now shows the More choices too: the rail's side, a floating bar, the bar's background, how the screen you're on is marked, names, icon and title sizes, the cover's shape, size and shadow, the seek bar's thickness, its times and swiping the cover.",
    "- **Colour blends on your own style:** in Make your own visualizer, the colour blend's preview draws the style you're making (from the style tab), not the Visualizer's style, so you see both together as you change the colours.",
    "- **The DJ's natural voice on the phone too, if you want it:** the phone keeps its own voice unless you get the PC's human-sounding one in DJ › Voice settings (about 130 MB, once; no internet needed after). Then you can pick either one there, or remove the download again.",
    "- **Update check at start:** each time the app opens it checks for an update and tells you whether there is one or not.",
    "- **Wrapped's top 15s fit on one screen:** the top songs, albums, EPs, singles and discoveries no longer run under the phone's buttons at the bottom.",
    "- **Your moods go everywhere:** every mood a song has (not just its main one) is saved in its file's MOOD tag, and Sync and backups carry them all, song by song, so your other device or a restored one has them without a scan.",
